From 745a618344ec761a4f7e69dd4b9ea1ec46c3c9e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 05yuki <ceu.azul.samu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:16:53 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] host-kv: DeepSeek-V4.1's KV pool covers the whole context,
 the compressed KV past the GPU's share in host memory

When the KV pool the GPU budget buys is shorter than the context, the pool
is made at the context length (1M tokens for V4.1-Flash-1017) instead. The
GPU keeps every byte but the ratio-1/2 compressed KV's (KVLayout.V41_FP4,
288 bytes an entry, kv_source layers 2/8/14/20): the index-K pools, which
decode scores in full at every index source, and as much of the compressed
KV as the budget leaves. The rest of the compressed KV lives in host memory
of the GPU's NUMA node. When the whole context fits the GPU nothing changes.

- Each ratio-1/2 pool layer is one kv_vmm range (kv_vmm_malloc_split): its
  first pages are device chunks, the rest host-NUMA chunks, so every writer
  and reader addresses it as before. A lent device chunk reads as zeros.
  Without kv_vmm a layer that cannot fit goes wholly to pinned host memory.
- The allocator hands out the lowest free pages first (freed pages go back
  in order), so requests fill the GPU's part before host memory.
- Decode: after each index source's top-k, a Triton kernel gathers its 512
  rows into a per-ratio device staging laid out as the pool's pages (the
  data, scale and page bytes read from the pool's own KVLayout, so V4, V41
  and V41_FP4 pools all work), and
  attention reads the staging with the rows renumbered; the following
  layers reuse it as they reuse the top-k. (Attention reading host memory
  in place costs ~100 us a layer; the gather is ~10 us an index source.)
- Prefill: the pool layer's pages up to the batch's highest slot are copied
  to the GPU at the first attention that reads them in the forward, after
  every writer (the bounded-replay tail rewrites the kv_source's entries),
  one layer's copy at a time (288 MB at 1M tokens), through an SM kernel (a
  range with host-NUMA chunks is not a valid cudaMemcpy source).
- The hot lend lends device pages only, and runs on the driver's spare alone
  when there is no device page to lend.

SGLANG_DSV41_HOST_KV=0 sizes the pool by the budget as before.

DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017, serve.sh defaults:
- two RTX 5070 Ti: the 1M pool fits, no host part; 24-piece NLL bit-identical
  to the previous build (2.5826).
- one RTX 5070 Ti: the pool goes from 180,480 to 1,048,576 tokens, the
  compressed KV all in host memory (0.70 GiB); decode 31.6 tok/s on Japanese
  prose (32.0 before), 35K prefill 776 tok/s (774); a 300K-token prompt
  prefills at 868 tok/s and decodes at 24.6 tok/s (24.7 at 8K, random ids);
  a 1M-token prompt prefills in 24.8 min and decodes at 23.8 tok/s.
- with hot experts fixed, the pools in host memory give an NLL bit-identical
  to the pools on the GPU, and the same greedy outputs on prompts up to
  8,417 tokens; with mem fraction 0.82 (the first 203,776 tokens' compressed
  KV on the GPU) a 300K-token prompt across the boundary prefills at 764 and
  decodes at 24.6 tok/s.
- the V4 layout (SGLANG_DSV4_KV_LAYOUT=v4) on one card: the pool at 1M with
  1.43 GiB in host memory gives the same greedy outputs on prompts up to
  8,417 tokens as the pool by the budget (89,344 tokens).

Prerequisites: kv-vmm, prefill-lend, stream-prefill, kv-lend-plan, hot-lend;
kv-vmm/kv_vmm.c with kv_vmm_malloc_split.

